# Pulse Deployment Environment Variables
# Reference only: every setting below is commented out. An unchanged copy
# configures nothing. Never overwrite an existing authentication file.
# Keep any edited deployment file private, outside version control, with
# owner-only permissions (chmod 600). Do not source it in a shell or share it.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compose interpolation (the bundled docker-compose.yml)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A .env beside docker-compose.yml supplies interpolation, not the container's
# environment. The bundled file consumes only PULSE_IMAGE, PULSE_PORT and TZ;
# placing other settings here does not pass them to Pulse.
# PULSE_IMAGE=rcourtman/pulse:vX.Y.Z
# PULSE_PORT=7655
# TZ=UTC
# Select an exact published image for your edition; see docs/DOCKER.md.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pulse runtime settings (not automatically forwarded by Compose)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pulse reads .env in its data directory: /etc/pulse for a default systemd
# install, /data inside a container, or the selected PULSE_DATA_DIR.
# Deployment-supplied environment values take precedence. Keep existing
# credentials, encryption keys and persistent data intact; do not replace an
# installation's .env with this example. See docs/CONFIGURATION.md.

# Authentication
# For a new install, leave PULSE_AUTH_USER and PULSE_AUTH_PASS unset and use
# browser bootstrap setup: docs/INSTALL.md#step-1-get-the-token.
# Headless automation: docs/CONFIGURATION.md#private-docker-authentication-file
# shows a private credential file for docker run, not a Compose interpolation
# recipe. Use a complete bcrypt hash; startup hashing does not remove a
# plaintext password from Docker's environment or your deployment file.
# API_TOKEN and API_TOKENS are ignored in v6. Create scoped tokens in
# Settings > API Access; see SECURITY.md#api-token-authentication.
# Never put a password or token in command arguments, a URL or a public report.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional security toggles
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PULSE_AUDIT_LOG=true

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Networking
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PULSE_PUBLIC_URL=https://pulse.example.com
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://pulse.example.com
# FRONTEND_PORT=7655
# BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Monitoring and logging
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DISCOVERY_SUBNET=192.168.50.0/24
# CONNECTION_TIMEOUT=10
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# METRICS_RETENTION_DAYS=7
